# Int and Float do not mix: f_loat, f_loor, c_eiling (Saga 27 step 3, D166).
== SOURCE
n := 3; u:g_ := { y -> y * 0.5 }; u:g_ n
== ERROR
error[type-mismatch]: expected Float, found Int
 --> -e:1:35
  |
1 | n := 3; u:g_ := { y -> y * 0.5 }; u:g_ n
  |                                   ^^^^^^
  |      - `n` gets its type here
  |                                        - `n` is an Int
  = help: Int and Float do not mix: `f_loat n` makes a Float of an Int, `f_loor x` or `c_eiling x` an Int of a Float
